{"id":"mahabharata-3-254","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":254,"title":"चतुःपञ्चाशदधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 254 · Draupadi points out her husbands","summary":{"en":"As the Pandavas charge, Jayadratha asks Draupadi who they are, and she proudly describes each of them, Yudhishthira, Bhima, Arjuna, Nakula and Sahadeva, and warns him of his doom. The Pandavas fall upon his army, sparing those who surrender.","kn":"ಪಾಂಡವರು ಮುನ್ನುಗ್ಗುವಾಗ ಅವರಾರೆಂದು ಜಯದ್ರಥನು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ದ್ರೌಪದಿ ಹೆಮ್ಮೆಯಿಂದ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ, ಭೀಮ, ಅರ್ಜುನ, ನಕುಲ, ಸಹದೇವರನ್ನು ಒಬ್ಬೊಬ್ಬರಾಗಿ ವರ್ಣಿಸಿ ಅವನ ವಿನಾಶದ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಎಚ್ಚರಿಸುತ್ತಾಳೆ. ಶರಣಾದವರನ್ನು ಬಿಟ್ಟು ಪಾಂಡವರು ಅವನ ಸೈನ್ಯದ ಮೇಲೆರಗುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"पाण्डवों के धावा बोलने पर जयद्रथ द्रौपदी से उनका परिचय पूछता है, और वे गर्व से युधिष्ठिर, भीम, अर्जुन, नकुल और सहदेव का एक-एक कर वर्णन करती हैं और उसे विनाश की चेतावनी देती हैं। पाण्डव शरणागतों को छोड़कर उसकी सेना पर टूट पड़ते हैं।","te":"పాండవులు దూసుకువస్తుండగా వారెవరని జయద్రథుడు అడుగుతాడు; ద్రౌపది గర్వంగా యుధిష్ఠిరుడు, భీముడు, అర్జునుడు, నకులుడు, సహదేవులను ఒక్కొక్కరిగా వర్ణించి అతని వినాశం గురించి హెచ్చరిస్తుంది. శరణుకోరినవారిని విడిచి పాండవులు అతని సైన్యంపై విరుచుకుపడతారు.","ta":"பாண்டவர்கள் பாய்ந்து வரும்போது அவர்கள் யார் என்று ஜயத்ரதன் கேட்க, திரௌபதி பெருமையுடன் யுதிஷ்டிரர், பீமன், அர்ஜுனன், நகுலன், ஸஹதேவனை ஒவ்வொருவராக வர்ணித்து அவன் அழிவை எச்சரிக்கிறாள். சரணடைந்தோரைத் தவிர்த்துப் பாண்டவர்கள் அவன் படை மீது பாய்கிறார்கள்.","ml":"പാണ്ഡവർ ആക്രമിക്കുമ്പോൾ ജയദ്രഥൻ ദ്രൗപദിയോട് അവർ ആരാണെന്ന് ചോദിക്കുന്നു; അഭിമാനത്തോടെ അവൾ ഓരോരുത്തരെയും വിവരിക്കുന്നു: യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ, ഭീമൻ, അർജുനൻ, നകുലൻ, സഹദേവൻ; അവന്റെ വിധി മുന്നറിയിപ്പായി നൽകുന്നു. പാണ്ഡവർ അവന്റെ സൈന്യത്തിന്മേൽ പതിക്കുന്നു, കീഴടങ്ങുന്നവരെ അവർ വെറുതെ വിടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.254; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"द्रौपदीहरणपर्व","titleEn":"Draupadiharana Parva (Abduction of Draupadi)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततो घोरतरः शब्दो वने समभवत्तदा ।\nभीमसेनार्जुनौ दृष्ट्वा क्षत्रियाणाममर्षिणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a terrible cry arose in the forest from the vengeful kshatriyas when they saw Bhimasena and Arjuna."}},{"n":2,"text":"तेषां ध्वजाग्राण्यभिवीक्ष्य राजा\nस्वयं दुरात्मा कुरुपुंगवानाम् ।\nजयद्रथो याज्ञसेनीमुवाच\nरथे स्थितां भानुमतीं हतौजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the tips of their banners, Jayadratha, the wicked king, spirits crushed, said to Draupadi, who stood in the chariot, radiant as the sun's light:"}},{"n":3,"text":"आयान्तीमे पञ्च रथा महान्तो\nमन्ये च कृष्णे पतयस्तवैते ।\nसा जानती ख्यापय नः सुकेशि\nपरं परं पाण्डवानां रथस्थम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Five great chariots are coming. I think these are your husbands, Krishna. You who know, fair-haired lady, tell me which Pandava is in which chariot, one after another.\""}},{"text":"द्रौपद्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Draupadi said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"किं ते ज्ञातैर्मूढ महाधनुर्धरै-\nरनायुष्यं कर्म कृत्वातिघोरम् ।\nएते वीराः पतयो मे समेता\nन वः शेषः कश्चिदिहास्ति युद्धे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fool, what use is it to you to know these great archers, when you have done a deed that will shorten your life? Here are my husbands, the heroes, gathered together; none of you will be left alive in the battle."}},{"n":5,"text":"आख्यातव्यं त्वेव सर्वं मुमूर्षो-\nर्मया तुभ्यं पृष्टया धर्म एषः ।\nन मे व्यथा विद्यते त्वद्भयं वा\nसंपश्यन्त्याः सानुजं धर्मराजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Still, this is the dharma: all must be told to you, who are about to die, since you ask. I feel no pain and no fear of you, seeing Dharmaraja with his brothers."}},{"n":6,"text":"यस्य ध्वजाग्रे नदतो मृदङ्गौ\nनन्दोपनन्दौ मधुरौ युक्तरूपौ ।\nएतं स्वधर्मार्थविनिश्चयज्ञं\nसदा जनाः कृत्यवन्तोऽनुयान्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The one whose banner top carries the two sweet, fitting drums Nanda and Upananda, sounding, whom men with tasks always follow, who knows what is right and profitable by his own dharma,"}},{"n":7,"text":"य एष जाम्बूनदशुद्धगौरः\nप्रचण्डघोणस्तनुरायताक्षः ।\nएतं कुरुश्रेष्ठतमं वदन्ति\nयुधिष्ठिरं धर्मसुतं पतिं मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"that one, fair as pure Jambunada gold, with a prominent nose, slender and long-eyed, is called the best of the Kurus: Yudhishthira, son of Dharma, my husband."}},{"n":8,"text":"अप्येष शत्रोः शरणागतस्य\nदद्यात्प्राणान्धर्मचारी नृवीरः ।\nपरैह्येनं मूढ जवेन भूतये\nत्वमात्मनः प्राञ्जलिर्न्यस्तशस्त्रः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That dharma-following hero would even give his life to an enemy who came for refuge. Run to him quickly for your welfare, fool, with joined palms and weapons laid down."}},{"n":9,"text":"अथाप्येनं पश्यसि यं रथस्थं\nमहाभुजं शालमिव प्रवृद्धम् ।\nसंदष्टोष्ठं भ्रुकुटीसंहतभ्रुवं\nवृकोदरो नाम पतिर्ममैषः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And this one you see in the chariot, mighty-armed, grown tall like a sala tree, biting his lip with his brows knit, is Vrikodara, my husband."}},{"n":10,"text":"आजानेया बलिनः साधु दान्ता\nमहाबलाः शूरमुदावहन्ति ।\nएतस्य कर्माण्यतिमानुषाणि\nभीमेति शब्दोऽस्य गतः पृथिव्याम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Strong horses of good breed, well trained, carry that hero. His deeds are superhuman, and the name Bhima has spread through the earth."}},{"n":11,"text":"नास्यापराद्धाः शेषमिहाप्नुवन्ति\nनाप्यस्य वैरं विस्मरते कदाचित् ।\nवैरस्यान्तं संविधायोपयाति\nपश्चाच्छान्तिं न च गच्छत्यतीव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who wrong him do not survive, and he never forgets an enmity; he sees the end of an enmity and goes after it, and afterward is never at rest."}},{"n":12,"text":"मृदुर्वदान्यो धृतिमान्यशस्वी\nजितेन्द्रियो वृद्धसेवी नृवीरः ।\nभ्राता च शिष्यश्च युधिष्ठिरस्य\nधनंजयो नाम पतिर्ममैषः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gentle, generous, steadfast, famous man who has conquered his senses and serves the elders, the hero, brother and pupil of Yudhishthira, is Dhananjaya, my husband."}},{"n":13,"text":"यो वै न कामान्न भयान्न लोभा-\nत्त्यजेद्धर्मं न नृशंसं च कुर्यात् ।\nस एष वैश्वानरतुल्यतेजाः\nकुन्तीसुतः शत्रुसहः प्रमाथी ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is one who would not give up dharma out of desire, fear or greed, and does nothing cruel. That son of Kunti has the radiance of fire, bears up against enemies and crushes them."}},{"n":14,"text":"यः सर्वधर्मार्थविनिश्चयज्ञो\nभयार्तानां भयहर्ता मनीषी ।\nयस्योत्तमं रूपमाहुः पृथिव्यां\nयं पाण्डवाः परिरक्षन्ति सर्वे ॥","meaning":{"en":"He knows what is right and useful in all matters of dharma, removes the fear of the frightened, is wise; they say he is the most beautiful on earth, and all the Pandavas protect him."}},{"n":15,"text":"प्राणैर्गरीयांसमनुव्रतं वै\nस एष वीरो नकुलः पतिर्मे ।\nयः खड्गयोधी लघुचित्रहस्तो\nमहांश्च धीमान्सहदेवोऽद्वितीयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is devoted and dearer than life: that hero Nakula is my husband, a swordsman of quick and skilled hands. And that great and wise one, Sahadeva, is without equal."}},{"n":16,"text":"यस्याद्य कर्म द्रक्ष्यसे मूढसत्त्व\nशतक्रतोर्वा दैत्यसेनासु संख्ये ।\nशूरः कृतास्त्रो मतिमान्मनीषी\nप्रियंकरो धर्मसुतस्य राज्ञः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You will see the deed of him today, fool, as of Indra in battle against the Daitya armies: brave, skilled in weapons, wise and intelligent, who does what pleases King Yudhishthira."}},{"n":17,"text":"य एष चन्द्रार्कसमानतेजा\nजघन्यजः पाण्डवानां प्रियश्च ।\nबुद्ध्या समो यस्य नरो न विद्यते\nवक्ता तथा सत्सु विनिश्चयज्ञः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who shines like the moon and sun, the youngest of the Pandavas, beloved, whose equal in intellect no man has, who speaks and decides well among the good,"}},{"n":18,"text":"स एष शूरो नित्यममर्षणश्च\nधीमान्प्राज्ञः सहदेवः पतिर्मे ।\nत्यजेत्प्राणान्प्रविशेद्धव्यवाहं\nन त्वेवैष व्याहरेद्धर्मबाह्यम् ।\nसदा मनस्वी क्षत्रधर्मे निविष्टः\nकुन्त्याः प्राणैरिष्टतमो नृवीरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"that brave, ever-impatient, wise and learned Sahadeva is my husband. He would give up his life or enter fire, but he would never say a thing outside dharma. Always high-minded and firm in kshatriya dharma, he is dearest to Kunti as her life."}},{"n":19,"text":"विशीर्यन्तीं नावमिवार्णवान्ते\nरत्नाभिपूर्णां मकरस्य पृष्ठे ।\nसेनां तवेमां हतसर्वयोधां\nविक्षोभितां द्रक्ष्यसि पाण्डुपुत्रैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You will see this army of yours, all its warriors killed and thrown into confusion by the sons of Pandu, falling apart like a ship full of jewels on a sea-monster's back at the edge of the ocean."}},{"n":20,"text":"इत्येते वै कथिताः पाण्डुपुत्रा\nयांस्त्वं मोहादवमन्य प्रवृत्तः ।\nयद्येतैस्त्वं मुच्यसेऽरिष्टदेहः\nपुनर्जन्म प्राप्स्यसे जीव एव ॥","meaning":{"en":"These are the sons of Pandu I have named for you, whom you have set out to scorn in your delusion. If you are freed by them with your body unharmed, you will gain a new birth while still alive.\""}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":21,"text":"ततः पार्थाः पञ्च पञ्चेन्द्रकल्पा-\nस्त्यक्त्वा त्रस्तान्प्राञ्जलींस्तान्पदातीन् ।\nरथानीकं शरवर्षान्धकारं\nचक्रुः क्रुद्धाः सर्वतः संनिगृह्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the five Pandavas, like the five Indras, left the frightened foot-soldiers with joined hands, and in anger closed in on all sides and made the chariot force dark with showers of arrows."}}]}]}